      {
        "description": "Fig. 3. Natural production of silk. Stage 1: in the posterior silk gland (PSG), the fibroin complex is assembled from its three components (the light and heavy fibroin\nchains and the glycoprotein P25). Stage 2: in the middle silk gland (MSG), a sericin coating is deposited on the fibroin complex to form the silk protein. Stage 3: in the\nanterior silk gland (ASG), silk fibers are assembled from individual silk protein complexes. Stage 4: silk fibers are matured in Filippi's glands. Stage 5: silk fibers are\nspun and secreted from the spinneret. (Adapted from [25]).",
        "label": "Fig 3.jpg",
